„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections•…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙZThe burden of Moab. Because in the night Ar of Moab is laid waste, and brought to silence;¦layout ‚¤textÙGBecause in the night Kir of Moab is laid waste, and brought to silence;¦layout©paragraphªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«He is gone up to Bajith, and to Dibon, the high places, to weep: Moab shall howl over Nebo, and over Medeba: on all their heads shall be baldness, and every beard cut off.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜In their streets they shall gird themselves with sackcloth: on the tops of their houses, and in their streets, every one shall howl, weeping abundantly.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨And Heshbon shall cry, and Elealeh: their voice shall be heard even unto Jahaz: therefore the armed soldiers of Moab shall cry out; his life shall be grievous unto him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙêMy heart shall cry out for Moab; his fugitives shall flee unto Zoar, an heifer of three years old: for by the mounting up of Luhith with weeping shall they go it up; for in the way of Horonaim they shall raise up a cry of destruction.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuFor the waters of Nimrim shall be desolate: for the hay is withered away, the grass faileth, there is no green thing.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~Therefore the abundance they have gotten, and that which they have laid up, shall they carry away to the brook of the willows.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|For the cry is gone round about the borders of Moab; the howling thereof unto Eglaim, and the howling thereof unto Beerelim.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™For the waters of Dimon shall be full of blood: for I will bring more upon Dimon, lions upon him that escapeth of Moab, and upon the remnant of the land.¦layout ªlast_verse	